{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T15:24:03.809Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d45976957f9ffc0b6cea979","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T15:24:03.809Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-31T15:24:03.809Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"Revert proof: with the previous pattern, 'home path detection refuses absolute homes and allows relative names and prose' and 'identity policy admits prose that only resembles a root home path' fail (5 pass / 2 fail); with the fix 7/7 pass. Test fixtures and this item's text build or describe home paths without writing one, so the commit passes its own gate. Same detector shape as pm-review's already-fixed gate, applied as an edit to pm-swarm's own file. The six other copies with the old pattern are tracked in the companion (pm-cli-website-hv91). Gates: 957/957 tests, coverage 100/100/100/100 over 37 files, docstrings 187."}]}],"before_hash":"97c62b539dae5396ca13e78ba1a5aba1d06916d11529ad5bdc2be65d36378045","after_hash":"cdc7c07bba9aa0b319fb6dc97933879dfc68f6ac7cdbed10911deb3678f1ee44","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"81b23f4abe5eb942744a7299d6347ddbfcde88c3bafaf8843c99f6fa8408813b"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T16:13:56.243Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d45976957f9ffc0b6cea979","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T16:13:56.242Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"CodeRabbit round on 4d2e829 (thread PRRT_kwDOVLY-P86ySTG_, two Major findings, both valid). (1) The exclusion lookbehind treated any non-ASCII or punctuation character as a token boundary, so relative paths whose previous component ends in such a character (a CJK folder name, c++) were refused. (2) A file://localhost URL slipped through, because its path slash follows a letter. Fix: a positive path-start boundary (line start, a leading diff marker, whitespace, quotes, opening brackets, assignment/list separators, emphasis, file:// and file://localhost); the audit strips the patch marker before testing. Revert proof: the new corpora fail with 4d2e829's detector (first failure: the file://localhost case); a direct check shows the old pattern refusing both relative cases. 7/7 identity tests pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T16:13:56.243Z"}],"before_hash":"cdc7c07bba9aa0b319fb6dc97933879dfc68f6ac7cdbed10911deb3678f1ee44","after_hash":"d1517fe4bf5b05c4e29a74f48667478f0d1c01d74e31d0b8b278d93647a76fd7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b12a0c27d31899e5b6d132a6a665b81c0474def5b5056a2cd41d4a71f152284d"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T17:20:01.323Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d45976957f9ffc0b6cea979","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T17:20:01.323Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"CodeRabbit round 2 on 228412f: four Major findings in three threads, all valid. Missed: home paths glued to command options (the cc include and ld library flags) and repeated leading slashes, both regressions against the original detector. Wrongly refused: a remote URL's query value. Missed: Windows profiles in another letter case. Fix, closing the neighbors too: any single-letter option glued to the path is a boundary; one or more leading slashes; homes and the root home below a var directory (Fedora Silverblue, macOS); remote URLs of any scheme of two or more characters except file are blanked before matching; the Windows profile matches any case. The macOS Users form stays case-sensitive on purpose, because a lowercase users segment is usually a web route (corpus case: a GET route for the current user). Revert proof: the round-2 corpora fail with the 228412f detector (first failure: the include-flag case); a direct check shows it missing the include flag and the doubled slash, and refusing the redirect query value. 7/7 identity tests pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T17:20:01.323Z"}],"before_hash":"d1517fe4bf5b05c4e29a74f48667478f0d1c01d74e31d0b8b278d93647a76fd7","after_hash":"e57e265c967376aeb0e83259c211c3d9d9d95662da6af3116818d8aacdfc8a79","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f975d5e6f05bbbd0e0633bc3b6d41d927b2b2f62d24bbe9ef722e1b8fbae7407"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T18:28:13.547Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d45976957f9ffc0b6cea979","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T18:28:13.547Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"CodeRabbit round 3 on 0dbcbfd: two findings, both valid. Major: URI schemes are case-insensitive, so an upper-case file scheme was masked as a remote URL and its home path slipped through. The file and localhost authorities in the path-start boundary were case-sensitive too. Minor: the remote-URL mask stopped at an opening parenthesis, a valid URL path character, so the rest of such a URL reached the detector. Fix: the remote-URL mask uses the i flag (so the file exception is case-insensitive) and ends only at a closing parenthesis, which still ends a Markdown link; the file and localhost authorities match any case. Revert proof: the round-3 corpus fails with 0dbcbfd's detector (first failure: the upper-case file URL). 7/7 identity tests pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T18:28:13.547Z"}],"before_hash":"e57e265c967376aeb0e83259c211c3d9d9d95662da6af3116818d8aacdfc8a79","after_hash":"3e8ce42a4ebe1564d8e0daa23dfe6ca3e44a61f6c55230dc593a1af836e65497","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"cbb240f6a9a226711cc438f97b2270590130a29c90cb22f37b87701ec8784a09"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T19:49:59.117Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0d45976957f9ffc0b6cea979","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T19:49:59.115Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","text":"CodeRabbit round 4 on 6f57ea5: one Major finding, valid. A single-letter option glued to a home path was only a path start after a line start, whitespace, a quote or an opening bracket, so an option inside an assignment (a CFLAGS-style variable) or a list (a linker -Wl option list) was missed. The option branch now also accepts assignment and list separators before the option. Corpus: three such cases; they fail with 6f57ea5's detector (first failure: the CFLAGS case). 7/7 identity tests pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T19:49:59.117Z"}],"before_hash":"3e8ce42a4ebe1564d8e0daa23dfe6ca3e44a61f6c55230dc593a1af836e65497","after_hash":"a3481e1944852b56557caef07b06ed77eaee7e17f9ad9c66f514a95cd0b24982","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"11a5d43eb5ab0e2515fef082e26849ce2c30a1021b6744da31459bbb8a161b30"}
